  "zipball_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/wentbackward/nv-monitor/zipball/v1.15.0",
  "body": "## What's changed\n\n### Bug fixes\n\n- **Headless `peak_30m` metrics were always 0.** With `-n` (e.g. running as a systemd service), the 30-minute windowed peaks were never updated, so every `nv_*_peak_30m_*` Prometheus metric and `peak_30m_*` CSV column read 0. Peaks are now sampled in the headless loop as well, for both `-p` and `-l`. Thanks @gringus for reporting this (#42). (04efd02)\n- **TUI flickered on every refresh.** The screen was fully cleared on every frame. ncurses now only redraws what changed, which removes the flicker and cuts terminal output by about 80%. A full repaint still happens on resize, every 60s as a safety net, and on demand with the new **Ctrl-L** key. Thanks @meteoricfarm for the report and suggested fix (#43). (aee5cf1)\n\n**Full changelog:** https://github.com/wentbackward/nv-monitor/compare/v1.14.0...v1.15.0\n\n## Which binary should I download?\n\n| File | Use on |\n|------|--------|\n| `nv-monitor-linux-arm64` | Modern aarch64 Linux (Ubuntu 24.04+, glibc 2.39+). **DGX Spark.** |\n| `nv-monitor-linux-arm64-legacy` | Older aarch64 Linux (glibc 2.35+). **Jetson Orin / JetPack 5/6.** Also works on newer systems. |\n| `nv-monitor-linux-amd64` | x86_64 Linux with an NVIDIA GPU. |\n| `demo-load-linux-*` | Companion synthetic load generator for testing. Same platform rules as nv-monitor. |\n\nIf in doubt on arm64, pick `-legacy` — it works almost everywhere.\n\n",
